<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine weekly official crop progress.</title>
<headline>Argentine weekly official crop progress.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hot, dry weather has damaged large parts of the Argentine soy crop, and many lots in central southern Santa Fe have been abandoned as feed, the Agriculture Secretariat said in weekly crop report Thursday.</p>
<p>The Secretariat said that 30.8 percent of the crop had been harvested by April 18 and predicted eventual soybean output of 12.86 million tonnes. With the sunflower harvest 96.1 percent over, yields were lower than expected and output likely to total 5.17 million tonnes.</p>
<p>Maize harvesting was 54.5 percent over. Output should total 14.44 million tonnes but yields have suffered through lack of rains and virus attacks.  </p>
<p>Intended total planting (thousands of hectares) and the percentage already sown (year-earlier in brackets). Harvest levels (thousands of hectares) and as a percentage of planted area, (year-earlier in brackets).</p>
